mode: "100644"
text: "# Platform SEO Surfaces\n\nThe crown jewel: exactly what each platform indexes for search, and how to optimize each. The point\nis that **the SEO surface differs per platform** — give platform-specific guidance, never one generic\nanswer.\n\n> Re-verify quarterly; indexed fields and search features evolve.\n\n## TikTok — audio + on-screen + caption\n\nA primary search engine for Gen Z. TikTok **transcribes spoken audio** and **reads on-screen text**, so\nthe technique is the **triple mention** (see `keyword-research-and-technique.md`):\n\n- **Spoken audio** — say the primary keyword **clearly, in the first few seconds.**\n- **On-screen text** — show the keyword as a headline overlay (keywords, not decorative text).\n- **Caption** — captions now allow long text (~thousands of chars); write it like a **searchable\n  description** (TikTok weighs the description over the comments), primary phrase early.\n- **Hashtags** — a category signal (3–5 niche), not the lever → `hashtag-strategy`.\n- Research: TikTok **autocomplete**, the **\"others searched for\"** carousel, Creative Center.\n\n## Instagram — caption + the name field + alt text\n\nKeyword search now outranks hashtags for discovery. Indexed surfaces:\n\n- **Name / display-name field** — *separately searchable from the @handle and heavily weighted.* Put\n  your core keyword/category here (e.g., \"Maya · Vegan Meal Prep\"), not just your name.\n- **Caption** — primary keyword in natural language, early (wins the search match + the see-more).\n- **On-screen text & audio** — increasingly read (caption your Reels).\n- **Alt text** — add descriptive, keyword-aware alt text (SEO + accessibility).\n- **Bio** — searchable; lead with the value prop + keyword.\n- Public **professional accounts are now Google-indexable** — captions/alt text travel.\n- Hashtags capped at **5** → `hashtag-strategy`.\n\n## YouTube — the deepest SEO surface\n\nThe 2nd-largest search engine, integrated with Google. Optimize, in order of weight:\n\n- **Title** — keyword-led and *descriptive* (\"How to Build a Content Calendar in Notion\" beats a vague\n  curiosity hook in search). Front-load the phrase.\n- **Description** — treat as a **200–300 word short article**: natural keyword-rich context, related\n  questions, links. Feeds in-platform *and* Google.\n- **Transcript / closed captions** — indexed; upload accurate captions (don't rely on auto only).\n- **Chapters / timestamps** — descriptive labels (\"02:10 What Social SEO Is\") help YouTube index\n  segments and can appear as **Google rich results.**\n- **Tags + descriptive file name** — supporting signals. **Thumbnail** drives CTR (a ranking input).\n- Applies to **Shorts and long-form**. Research: YouTube autocomplete (seed + wildcard), TubeBuddy/VidIQ.\n\n## Pinterest — a pure keyword search engine\n\nThe most search-driven platform; **hashtags are largely deprecated → keywords are the whole game.**\n\n- **Pin title + description** — keyword-rich, descriptive, intent-matching.\n- **Board names + descriptions** — keyword-organized (boards are topic clusters).\n- **Alt text + on-image text** — describe the pin in searchable terms.\n- Pinterest content is evergreen and surfaces for months — strong for inspiration/planning intent.\n\n## LinkedIn — profile + topic keywords\n\nA top B2B search/discovery surface:\n\n- **Profile** — the **headline and About are heavily searchable**; lead with niche + value keywords.\n- **Post keywords** — feed the **topic-matching** (\"topic DNA\") that distributes you to the right\n  professionals (search + recommendation overlap). Stay in your lane → `linkedin-growth`.\n- 3–5 niche hashtags as supporting signals.\n\n## X / Facebook (briefly)\n\n- **X** — real-time keyword search; **bio + post text searchable**, indexed by Google; 1–2 hashtags.\n- **Facebook** — local-business / group / community search; complete the Page fields with keywords.\n\n## Cross-cutting (every platform)\n\n- **Subtitles / captions** on every video — indexed *and* most people watch sound-off.\n- **Alt text** wherever supported — searchable + accessible.\n- **Descriptive file names** before upload.\n- **Profile fields** — a **consistent branded handle** (append a keyword/location if taken:\n  `@oakandlinen.home`); searchable name/display field; keyword-aware bio.\n- **Native uploads** (not links to other platforms) get preferential treatment.\n"
